 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Start with base of light red, then build up in thin layers until it feels smooth. Mix the last bit with a little of the base color, not the whole thing. Start with the same base, and mix in touch more yellow or blue until you get the right shade. Mix small batches for skin, you' never use it all. A large pot gets hard and hard to mix evenly. Use a full size brush for portraits, and hold it at quarter to half angle. A flat brush gives flat shadows.",
